      "statusChangeID": "5d23ac24a42db3220da5cd62",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "@{59b05781f76da93741a4617e|full_name}, thanks for the feedback! We've discussed this internally and have decided to hold off on adding a global voice falloff option. We're concerned that this option is often used incorrectly and breaks voice in worlds. And since it's on the scene descriptor, is easily copy/pasted to other worlds and users.\n\nAs you mentioned, as a work around today, VRC_VoiceOverrideRegion can be used to set global falloff by creating a trigger that covers the entire world. Note that until priority is implemented, it is unexpected behaviour to have overlapping VRC_VoiceOverrideRegions. \n\nWe do expect to continue adding greater creator flexibility for audio!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
